# NHL Playoff Predictor - Project Context

## Project Purpose
Two-model system for 2026 NHL playoffs:
1. **Team Model (V2)** — Predict series winners across all 4 rounds using 25 years of historical data (2001-2025) with ensemble ML + Monte Carlo simulation.
2. **Scoring Model** — Predict individual playoff point totals for every skater on playoff/bubble teams, rank top 35 scorers. Built on team model's expected-games output.

## Architecture — Team Model
- `config/settings.py` — Central config (paths, API URLs, seasons `FIRST_SEASON=2001`..`LAST_HISTORICAL_SEASON=2025`, `CURRENT_SEASON_END_YEAR=2026`, `RANDOM_STATE`, team mappings)
- `src/data/nhl_api_client.py` — HTTP client with disk cache, rate limiting, retry. Constructor takes `cache_ttl_hours` (default 6.0). Methods: `_web()`, `_stats()`, `get_standings()`, `get_team_stats()`, `get_goalie_stats()`
- `src/data/collectors.py` — `collect_standings()`, `collect_team_stats_nhl()`, `collect_moneypuck_team_stats()`, `collect_goalie_stats()`. MoneyPuck uses `{start_year}` URL format. Standings use `today.isoformat()` for current season.
- `src/data/collectors_v2.py` — `collect_skater_stats()` (gameTypeId=2), `collect_moneypuck_recency()`, `collect_head_to_head()`, `collect_playoff_schedules()`
- `src/features/engineer.py` — `normalize_team()`, `_build_team_season_features()`, `_compute_differential()`, `_get_team_features()`
- `src/features/advanced.py` — V2 features: player-level, H2H, injury proxy, round, rest, style, conference, SOS. `integrate_advanced_features()` merges into main matrix.
- `src/features/elo.py` — ELO rating system for teams
- `src/models/trainer.py` — Baseline LogReg, XGB, LGB, voting ensemble
- `src/models/improved_trainer.py` — Temporal CV, multi-stage feature selection, StackingClassifier, CalibratedClassifierCV (uses `StratifiedKFold` not `TimeSeriesSplit` for internal CV)
- `src/models/bayesian.py` — `BayesianLogistic` class with uncertainty estimates
- `src/models/monte_carlo.py` — `simulate_series(base_prob, n_sims=50000)` returns dict with `series_win_prob`, `expected_games`, sweep/5/6/7 game probs. `simulate_bracket()`, `print_bracket_results()`
- `scripts/run_v2_pipeline.py` — Master pipeline: `step_collect()`, `step_features()`, `step_train_v2()`, `step_predict_v2()`. Supports `--predict-only`.

## Architecture — Scoring Model
- `src/data/collectors_playoff_scoring.py` — `collect_playoff_skater_stats()` (gameTypeId=3), `collect_regular_season_skater_stats()` (gameTypeId=2), `collect_player_bios()` (birthDate, draft info from `/skater/bios`). Saves to `data/raw/skater_stats_playoffs.csv`, `skater_stats_regular_historical.csv`, `player_bios.csv`.
- `src/data/roster_injury.py` — `fetch_live_standings()`, `compute_playoff_probabilities()`, `identify_contender_teams()`, `fetch_team_roster()`, `check_player_activity()`, `verify_and_flag_players()`. Inactivity threshold: 14 days.
- `src/features/player_scoring.py` — `build_training_dataset()`, `build_prediction_features()`, `_extract_player_features()` (53 features), `_compute_team_scoring_ranks()`, `_compute_team_playoff_games()`, `_build_bios_lookup()`, `_build_team_stats_lookup()`. Accepts `player_bios_df` and `team_stats_df` for age/team context features. `PLAYOFF_DISCOUNT` dict maps position to historical playoff/regular scoring ratio.
- `src/models/scoring_predictor.py` — `train_scoring_models()` (Ridge + XGBoost + LightGBM regressors with log-transform targets), `_train_gate_classifier()` (LogReg for P(scores>0)), `_train_stacking_meta()` (Ridge meta-learner on OOF predictions + gate prob), `temporal_cv_splits()`, `predict_blended()` (accepts gate + meta_model), `get_feature_importance()`. RandomizedSearchCV with `n_iter=100`, `TimeSeriesSplit(n_splits=5)`. Sample weights: `0.88^(max_season - season)`. Auto-selects between stacking meta and Dirichlet+gate blend.
- `scripts/run_scoring_pipeline.py` — Master pipeline: `step_collect()`, `step_compute_team_expected_games()` (returns `(team_games, team_probs)` tuple), `step_build_and_train()`, `step_predict()`. Supports `--predict-only`. Predict-only always recomputes team expected games for freshest standings.

## Key Data Sources
- **NHL Web API** (`api-web.nhle.com/v1`) — Standings (`/standings/now`), rosters (`/roster/{team}/current`), player game logs (`/player/{id}/game-log/{seasonId}/{gameType}`)
- **NHL Stats API** (`api.nhle.com/stats/rest/en`) — Team stats (`/team/{report}`), skater stats (`/skater/{report}`), goalie stats (`/goalie/{report}`). Filter by `cayenneExp=gameTypeId=2` (regular) or `=3` (playoff).
- **MoneyPuck** (`moneypuck.com/moneypuck/playerData/seasonSummary/{start_year}/regular/teams.csv`) — Advanced analytics. Requires browser-like headers.

