## Key Debugging History
- **MoneyPuck 403/404**: Required browser-like User-Agent/Referer headers; URL uses `{start_year}` not `{season_id}`
- **teamAbbrev dict**: NHL API returns `{'default': 'COL'}` — parse with `x.get("default")` or `eval(x)` for cached string version
- **All-NaN features**: Drop columns >80% NaN before feature selection (pre-MoneyPuck era gap)
- **StackingClassifier CV**: Must use `StratifiedKFold(shuffle=False)` not `TimeSeriesSplit` for internal CV
- **Empty training data**: Regular season stats file only had 2026 data; needed to collect 25-year historical file separately (`skater_stats_regular_historical.csv`)
- **RandomizedSearchCV n_iter**: Reduced from 200 to 80 to avoid timeout during 3-target x 3-model training (~8 min total)
- **PowerShell quoting**: Inline Python strings with quotes and braces need careful escaping; use single-line commands or script files
- **Unicode errors**: Replace `→` with `=>` in print statements; set `$env:PYTHONIOENCODING = "utf-8"`

## Known Issues / Gotchas
- MoneyPuck `teams_20.csv` (recency) only available from ~2024 onwards
- NHL API `teamAbbrev` field returns `{'default': 'COL'}` dict — must extract correctly
- Some features are all-NaN for early seasons (pre-MoneyPuck era) — drop >80% NaN cols before selection
- Team model imputer warnings for missing features in single-matchup inference — harmless but noisy
- LGBMRegressor "X does not have valid feature names" warning during scoring prediction — harmless
- Goals + assists reconciliation: final points = average of (direct points prediction) and (predicted goals + predicted assists)
- Scoring pipeline `--predict-only` still recomputes team expected games for fresh standings data
- Log-transform models: Slightly higher individual-model MAE in original space is expected trade-off for better ranking (Spearman). Stacking meta-learner recovers MAE.
- `team_standings_pts` feature is NaN in training data (no standings available for historical team-player joins). Imputed by median. Available for current-season predictions.
- Player bios collection takes ~25 API calls (one per season). Cached to `player_bios.csv`.
- Noisy expected games in training (V3 fix): Adds ~1.8 games/round Gaussian noise to actuals. This intentionally increases MAE slightly but produces predictions that generalize better at inference time.
- Position calibration factors near ceiling (F=1.29, D=1.30): Both hit the 1.3 cap, suggesting the model still systematically underpredicts. May need to investigate whether log-transform + gate interaction causes systematic underestimation.
- Bootstrap CI width varies significantly (MacKinnon: 19.3-39.4 = 20.1 pt range vs Brayden Point: 4.8-5.7 = 0.9 pt range) — wider for high-scoring players as expected from multiplicative uncertainty.

## Remaining Potential Improvements
- **Game-by-game historical data**: Use individual game logs for recent form features (last 10/20 game scoring rates)
- **Linemate/deployment data**: Who plays on PP1 vs PP2, top-6 vs bottom-6
- **Round-by-round scoring decay**: Explicit per-round scoring adjustment (R1 higher than SCF)
- **Coaching/system effects**: Offensive vs defensive coaching styles
- **Mid-season trade handling**: Players who changed teams mid-season
